We honor the sacrifices made by those who fought for the abolition of slavery and stand in solidarity with those currently fighting for racial justice and equity.

We pledge to work tirelessly to ensure that every individual, regardless of background, enjoys full citizenship rights and protections under the law.

Let us strive together to build a more just and equitable society where everyone can thrive without fear of oppression or exploitation.

In this spirit, we call upon all citizens to educate themselves about the history of slavery and its lasting impacts, and to actively participate in efforts to promote social justice and equality for all.

Let us remember that the struggle for true freedom and equality is ongoing, and that progress requires constant vigilance and dedication from all members of our community.

Let us honor the memory of those who fought for the abolition of slavery and commit to building a future where every person is treated with dignity and respect, regardless of their past experiences.

IN WITNESS WHEREOF, I, [Your Name], President of the United States, sign this resolution on behalf of the United States Government.

[Date]

